Measured, not written (G24 round 3): the iOS a11y sweep's lines for the Form on the shipped code, iOS 27. The row with `onPress` holds two Texts; the React Native wrapper for the labelled one carries the app's name, and nothing else does - the list's cell does not answer for the row's name, so the row is not one element to a screen reader.
The third line is the element around the wrapper, read by a probe that looked for it (round 2): the row's own box, no label, not a button. The shipped sweep prints the first two lines only; both readings give the same verdict.
